From 0d00238be2f00061aa18bae1d1ac697a27e9e8d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:52:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): event order trusts a uid minted just past
 created_at's second [daveey]

`consistent_uid_milliseconds(uid, seconds)` trusted a v7 uid's ms only
inside the row's own created_at second. created_at is `int(time.time())`
read in Python before the INSERT, while the uid is minted by the AFTER
INSERT trigger, so a write straddling a second boundary carries a
legitimate uid in second+1. Such an event fell back to second*1000 and
sorted before consistent-uid events of the same second: in
`kanban_sync_divergence._event_order` (the terminal guard's
`terminal_hold` order) a straddled terminal could sort before an earlier
same-second reopen and drop the hold (fail-open), or a straddled reopen
before an earlier terminal and keep a hold that should drop. The same
rule feeds `kanban_shared_blockers._event_order`.

The window is now [seconds*1000, (seconds+1)*1000 + UID_STRADDLE_MS)
with UID_STRADDLE_MS = 1000; a uid stamped further out (a backfill) is
still distrusted and the local id decides. Non-int seconds return None.
`_uid_before_check` is unaffected: a claim minted in second+1 is never
before a check of second `started`, so it keeps its fallback.

Evidence (read-only replay, 12 kanban DBs on worker-6: kanban.db,
boards/*, sync-shadow/*; 957,626 v7 event uids), uid ms minus
created_at*1000:
- [0, 1000): 831,590; [1000, 2000): 296 (285 unique-ms singletons,
  i.e. trigger-minted; overshoot p50 1 ms, p90 58, p99 579, max 760);
- [2000, 60000): 78 (68 shared-ms backfill batches); >= 60 s: 125,355
  (125,354 batches: backfills).

Follow-up from review t_01a1db0f0278c8dc of PR #3045 (nit 1);
card t_01a1db15eb8f8cb6.

Proof:
- RED on dda3fd767515 (old fence, new tests): 9 failed across
  test_kanban_shared_blocker_uid_precision (window, shared-blocker
  _event_order), test_kanban_stale_wake_terminal (straddled terminal
  after same-second reopen, mirror) and test_kanban_sync_running_heal
  (_event_order window).
- GREEN: those 3 files pass; the backfill tests (uid >= second+2, incl.
  the existing 900 s case) still fall back to id order. Every test file
  importing kanban_sync_divergence, kanban_terminal_guard or
  kanban_shared_blocker*: 37 files, 950 passed.
- Mutants killed (5/5): lower bound < , upper bound <=, window 0, window
  2000, dropped int guard.
- Replay old vs new over the same 12 DBs: terminal_hold changed for 0
  of 17,210 tasks; _unblocked_since_assertion changed for 0 of 204
